   "mbody",
   "<p class=\"ui-lead\">Compare this fingerprint with the source host's own console before allowing Homestead to log in.</p><div class=\"ui-callout warn\" role=\"alert\">\n      <span class=\"ui-callout-icon\"><svg class=\"ui-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#i-alert\"/></svg></span>\n      <div><b>A scan is not proof of identity</b><div class=\"ui-callout-body\"><p class=\"ui-issue\"><span class=\"ui-issue-short\">Use the host's physical console or an already trusted management session, not this new SSH connection.</span></p></div></div>\n    </div><dl class=\"ui-facts\"><div><dt>Host</dt><dd>192.0.2.10:22</dd></div><div><dt>Host key</dt><dd>ssh-ed25519</dd></div></dl><section class=\"ui-section\">\n    <header><h4>Compare fingerprint</h4></header>\n    <div class=\"mono\" style=\"overflow-wrap:anywhere\">SHA256:fixture</div></section><section class=\"ui-section\">\n    <header><h4>On the source console</h4></header>\n    <code style=\"overflow-wrap:anywhere\">ssh-keygen -lf /etc/ssh/ssh_host_ed25519_key.pub</code></section><details class=\"ui-more\" data-disclosure=\"What trusting changes\">\n    <summary>What trusting changes</summary><div class=\"ui-more-body\"><p>New discovery and copy connections must match this key. A key change stops new connections; it is never accepted automatically. Existing helpers retain the key and credentials they started with.</p></div></details><label class=\"ui-ack\">\n    <input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"sourceKeyAck\" onchange=\"sourceKeyReady()\"><span>I compared this fingerprint with the source host's console.</span></label><div class=\"ui-actions\" >\n      <div class=\"ui-actions-start\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"btn\" onclick=\"closeModal()\" data-dialog-dismiss=\"true\">Not now</button></div><div class=\"ui-actions-end\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"btn pri\" id=\"sourceKeyApply\" onclick=\"sourceKeyTrust()\" disabled >Trust this source</button></div></div>"
  ],
